-- title:
--   Chart rings of the two-chart model are integrally closed
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $F$ be a field carrying an $R$-algebra structure, and let $S$ be an arbitrary subset of $F$. Write $R[S] =$ `Algebra.adjoin R S` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $S$, and let `chartAlg R F S` be the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ whose underlying set is $\{x \in F : x \text{ is integral over } R[S]\}$ (closed under sums, products, containing $0$ and $1$ and the image of $R$, by the usual closure properties of integral elements). The theorem asserts that the ring `chartAlg R F S`, viewed as a type via its coercion, is integrally closed, i.e. every element of its fraction field which is integral over it already lies in the image of `chartAlg R F S`. No hypothesis whatever is imposed on $R$ beyond commutativity, none on the $R$-algebra structure of $F$, and none on $S$; in particular $S$ may be empty, in which case the assertion is that the integral closure of the image of $R$ in $F$ is integrally closed.
--
--   This is the normality statement for the affine charts of the two-chart integral model: taking $S = \{j\}$ and $S = \{j^{-1}\}$ gives that both chart rings `chartAlgFin` and `chartAlgInf` are integrally closed domains. It is used downstream for the integral closedness of the local rings of the model and, through that, for reducedness and normality properties of the glued scheme.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_isIntegrallyClosed_chartAlg.lean

